{"name":"Chestnut Dressing","hex":"#ebc795","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chestnut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible nut (technically a fruit) of the Spanish chestnut or sweet chestnut tree (Castanea sativa); also (chiefly preceded by a descriptive word), a nut from a related shrub or tree; or a similar nut from an unrelated plant.","In full chestnut tree: the shrub or tree that bears this nut, the Spanish chestnut or sweet chestnut (Castanea sativa); also (chiefly preceded by a descriptive word), a shrub or tree of the genus Castanea."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep reddish-brown colour, like that of a chestnut fruit (noun sense 1)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chestnut"},{"term":"dressing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Material applied to a wound for protection or therapy.","A sauce, especially a cold one for salads."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of dress"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dressing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stuffing","blocks":[{"text":"Stuffing, filling, or dressing is an edible mixture, often composed of herbs and a starch such as bread, used to fill a cavity in the preparation of another food item. Many foods may be stuffed, including poultry, seafood, and vegetables. As a cooking technique, stuffing helps retain moisture, while the mixture itself augments and absorbs flavors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Stuffing_a_turkey.jpg/330px-Stuffing_a_turkey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuffing"},{"title":"Chestnut","blocks":[{"text":"Chestnuts are the deciduous trees and shrubs in the genus Castanea, in the beech family Fagaceae. The name also refers to the edible nuts they produce. They are native to temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.